    ALIGNMENT CHECK  overall F1 sd 32.9 phase-locked vs 31.3 interpolated leak (+5.2%)
    ALIGNMENT -- total F1 movement is comparable while the per-cycle
    excursion is larger, so the gain is in WHEN the movement happens.
    THE PHASE STRUCTURE PAYS. At matched drift the cycle-locked gate carries
    more per-cycle range than a leak reaching the same drift, and a renamed
    position decoder cannot do that. Replicate on a fresh seed family before
    it is quoted -- one draw, and this project's standard is replication.

  --- the gate or the anchor? ---
    v62-nogate    (tau 633, no gate)  drift  132.5
    nogate+tau60  (tau  60, no gate)  drift   59.9
    thin+tau60    (tau  60, GATED)    drift   29.4
    the short anchor alone accounts for 70% of the bounding
    THE GATE IS DOING THE WORK. The same anchor without the phase gate
    leaves most of the drift in place, so the gate is what lets the anchor
    act -- the creature is voiced too much of the time for an idle-only
    anchor to bound anything.

